{"base_rate":0.2073976221928666,"brier":0.14125112285336855,"bss":0.1407238354564757,"bss_hi":0.2770435617233961,"bss_lo":-0.024755453797343643,"chart":{"base":[330.9,70.2],"fp":[201.2,223.3],"lead":"62,248.5 272,220 482,173.4 692,109.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.14 — higher than 22% of cities","fp":"low end +0pp, high end +33pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 46% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 2%; promised 99% → rained 73%"},"rel":"63.3,458.8 146.3,437.2 440,379 682.7,152.6"},"country":"HU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1527212681638045,"ess":378.97713383012297,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Budapest</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Budapest rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>73%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nBUDAPEST, 2.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.14, ranked 167 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(112&ndash;188) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>300</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'><b>13%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'><b>28%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>153</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Budapest</b> <span class=\"muted\">Hungary</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.14</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>112&ndash;188\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Budapest &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Budapest\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.708,379.5733333333333 82.41692307692308,335.3333333333333 130.22583333333336,275.8333333333333 219.61461538461535,176.66666666666666 322.47526315789474,75.47368421052636 406.79411764705884,18.0 406.79411764705884,29.954901960784298 322.47526315789474,147.31578947368422 219.61461538461535,256.0 130.22583333333336,341.55555555555554 82.41692307692308,372.6666666666667 58.708,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"306.50726552179657\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"306.50726552179657\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.708,375.93333333333334 82.41692307692308,358.6666666666667 130.22583333333336,356.72222222222223 219.61461538461535,335.3333333333333 322.47526315789474,281.42105263157896 406.79411764705884,117.921568627451\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 300 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.708\" cy=\"375.93333333333334\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"82.41692307692308\" cy=\"358.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"130.22583333333336\" cy=\"356.72222222222223\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 46%&amp;#10;It rained 13% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"219.61461538461535\" cy=\"335.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 75%&amp;#10;It rained 28% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"322.47526315789474\" cy=\"281.42105263157896\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 73% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 153 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"406.79411764705884\" cy=\"117.921568627451\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(21%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Budapest the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.33) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.35).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>-0.349</td><td class='num'>20.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'>0.152</td><td class='num'>15.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.269</td><td class='num'>13.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.332</td><td class='num'>13.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":47.49835,"lon":19.04045,"n":757,"n_cities":213,"name":"Budapest","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.002,"n":300,"obs":0.016666666666666666,"sig":true},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.06897435897435898,"n":78,"obs":0.0641025